+## Selected data-plane contracts and Task 4 compatibility boundary
+
+Blob SDK `azure-storage-blob 12.31.0` supports explicit `api_version="2026-04-06"`, selected for every Blob client, including ADF GET `x-ms-version`. The tagged publisher `_serialize.py` supports it; `_shared/constants.py` chooses the last supported version by default (`2026-10-06`). Explicit version pin avoids that mutable/default discrepancy. Microsoft Storage versioning documents `2026-04-06` fully deployed, with newer versions enabled in the candidate US regions; documentation remains distinct from actual account proof. Tables SDK `azure-data-tables 12.7.0` supports `2019-02-02`, `2019-07-07`, `2020-12-06`; select explicit `api_version="2020-12-06"`. Tagged `_base_client.py` documents default 2019-02-02, so this pin is intentional. Publisher source/tag observations are not actual installed request traces. [Blob source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-python/azure-storage-blob_12.31.0/sdk/storage/azure-storage-blob/azure/storage/blob/_serialize.py), [Tables source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-python/azure-data-tables_12.7.0/sdk/tables/azure-data-tables/azure/data/tables/_base_client.py), [Storage versions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/versioning-for-the-azure-storage-services).
+
+| Data object / lifecycle | API selection, method/path and response requirement | Safeguard / limitation |
+|---|---|---|
+| Raw snapshots, observations, worksets, result reports, quarantine, generation Parquet, manifests, approval evidence | Blob only: PUT `https://{account}.blob.core.windows.net/{container}/{path}` (Put Blob); large BlockBlob upload uses PUT `?comp=block&blockid=...` then PUT `?comp=blocklist`; GET/HEAD same object for bytes/properties; responses/ETag/content hash retained by later implementation | New immutable paths/create-if-absent; verify exact final bytes/hash before manifest/approval/pointer. Never create these via DFS Path Create, NFS or portal tooling that changes the write API. No append/page blobs, DFS rename or recursive directory deletion dependency. |
+| Lock sentinel | Blob-created block blob; PUT `?comp=lease` acquire/renew/release/break (operator recovery only), GET/HEAD properties; lease ID in required leased writes | Lease excludes writes/deletes to that blob, not network traffic or Table writes. Parent lease-loss stop, bounded in-flight requests and takeover checks retained. |
+| Source/attempt/active-pointer/approval entity | Table GET `{table}(PartitionKey='...',RowKey='...')`; POST `{table}` insert; PUT or MERGE exact entity with actual opaque ETag in If-Match for replace/merge | Conditional update 204, mismatch 412; no wildcard `*`, missing If-Match or upsert as CAS. First insert conflicts must be reconciled. No atomic Blob+Table transaction assumed. |
+| Reader/ADF durable result | GET immutable exact Blob with Storage audience; reader pointer GET → exact manifest/data GET; ADF result is bounded JSON object below Web limit | Match execution/run/command/attempt/workset/digest; reader must not select newest blob or active generation by listing. |
+
+HNS mixing restriction applies per file instance: a DFS-created file cannot be overwritten with PutBlock/PutBlockList; PutBlob overwrite exception is size-limited and is unnecessary here. Final selection therefore retains Blob/Table only and the exact Task 4 21-distribution lock. No DFS dependency is added and no repeat probe is authorized/needed for this unchanged combination. This documents future operation intent, not SDK request/lifecycle correctness or actual HNS compatibility. A later DFS/rename requirement, different SDK pin or wheel composition reopens Task 4 and requires separately owner-authorized proof; four temporary runs are exhausted. See `provider/task5-storage/storage-source-notes.md` and [HNS restrictions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-known-issues).
+
+## Start, async, execution and durable-result decision table
+
+`turnOffAsync=true` is the selected design choice for the single start Web activity: expose initial acceptance so the application owns bounded observation rather than ADF's default unbounded-for-this-policy follow-up. Activity `retry=0`; explicit response timeout at most 10 minutes, default 1 minute unless separately chosen later. Default `turnOffAsync=false` automatically GETs Location and can wait up to seven days; it does not prove exact execution correlation, is not the selected polling mechanism, and cannot turn ARM acceptance into worker success. ADF Web requires JSON object responses and supports at most 4 MB output; 202/no-body, Location header exposure and final response shape remain Stage 7. If output does not expose sufficient data, operator recovery is required before any additional launch; no latest execution fallback. [ADF Web](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/control-flow-web-activity).
+
+| Observation | Application decision / retained correlation | Passing evidence required at Stage 7 |
+|---|---|---|
+| Start 200 with id/name | Validate exact execution ARM ID is under accepted subscription/RG/job `/executions/{name}`, matching name. Persist start receipt with ADF run ID, command, attempt, immutable workset ID/hash and image digest. Proceed exact execution GET; 200 means start completed, not work succeeded. | Actual initial payload/headers/output and durable correlation persisted without secrets; no invented execution ID. |
+| Start 202 with Location and Retry-After | Retain initial receipt; validate absolute HTTPS host exactly management.azure.com (no userinfo/nonstandard port/fragment), subscription/region/provider operation path and returned API version before authenticated GET. Honor longer server delay. ARM token audience only. Never forward token to arbitrary Location/redirect host. | Actual selected-version Location path/schema, exact permission and terminal result returning execution reference. Asynchronous-operation success alone insufficient. |
+| Azure-AsyncOperation header also returned | ARM general guidance prioritizes Azure-AsyncOperation over Location; unexpected selected Start header retained and validated before polling. No rewrite to assumed path or generic examples. | Observed operation-status/result endpoint mapping and schema for selected Jobs version; auxiliary guessed URLs failed and retained. |
+| Async ends with valid exact execution reference | Persist reference then exact GET; correlate unchanged workset/attempt/run/digest tuple. | ADF output proves reference came from this start. |
+| Missing id/header, timeout, lost response, GET unavailable, unexpected enum/schema, deadline | `execution_unknown`; retain evidence; fail closed/operator recovery; no start retry and no confirmed-transient replay from uncertainty. Exact list may aid recovery only with authoritative tuple proof; list-by-time/latest is never proof. | Ambiguous-start fault injection demonstrating no duplicate collector start. |
+| Exact status Succeeded | Candidate only: validate exact matching successful durable worker JSON and required publication/result checks. | Both ARM execution receipt and immutable successful result match entire tuple; contradictory/missing result fails. |
+| Confirmed failure | Failed result; at most one accepted confirmed-transient replay, after classification, lease/in-flight completion and durable same-workset new-attempt bookkeeping | Positive causal transient evidence and bounded replay proof; no idempotency inference from start response. |
+
+Proposed new application observation policy D-18: 30s base between status checks, honor longer server Retry-After, absolute 4,200s deadline from initial start issuance including async handling and 3,600s replica allowance. Deadline never implies termination; stop automatic observation and classify unknown/recover operationally. Provider/platform scheduling overhead can exhaust this budget before a replica finishes; it is an intentional bounded observer, not completion SLA. D-18 remains unaccepted pending owner decision. Jobs event pollingInterval (30s default) polls event sources, not execution status or ADF.
+
+ARM async guidance requires support for ≥4KB Location/AsyncOperation URLs and permissions beyond exact resource scope; actual path/region/provider operation read mapping remains Stage 7. Proposed permitted paths are exact job execution resources plus returned `Microsoft.App/locations/{selectedRegion}/containerappsjoboperationstatuses/{operationId}` or `...containerappsjoboperationresults/{operationId}` under accepted subscription, subject to verification of selected-version actual response. No arbitrary path/token forwarding is approved. General docs describe provider-varying status payloads; failed guessed reference URLs do not prove API absence. [ARM async](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/async-operations).
+
+## All seven execution states
+
+The selected GET documentation's meaning column merely repeats each enum label. Policy below is deliberately conservative; message/reason/endTime/container exit codes alone cannot override exact status or missing durable result.
+
+| State | Documented meaning | Policy | Stage 7 check |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Running | Running | Continue bounded observation | Exact GET and unchanged correlation |
+| Processing | Processing | Continue bounded observation | Demonstrate processing transition/handling |
+| Succeeded | Succeeded | Candidate success only with matching durable success | Missing/contradictory/mismatched result fails |
+| Failed | Failed | Failed; replay only if positively confirmed transient under one-replay contract | Failed durable evidence and classified replay |
+| Stopped | Stopped | Unsuccessful; no automatic transient inference | Stop receipt and result handling |
+| Degraded | Degraded | Uncertain, never passing or replay authorization | Selected-version behavior and conservative handling |
+| Unknown | Unknown | Uncertain/execution_unknown; operator recovery | Unknown handling, no second launch |
+
+Unrecognized enum, unavailable GET or observation deadline cannot pass; none authorizes transient replay. [Exact state schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/resource-manager/containerapps/job-execution/job-execution?view=rest-resource-manager-containerapps-2026-07-01).
+
+## Tools and retry rationale
+
+Proposed exact deployment tool contract: Azure CLI 2.90.0, Bicep CLI 0.38.33. CLI 2.90.0 and uv 0.12.15 were locally observed by root; Bicep and Docker/buildx are absent. Proposed future method is ACR quick tasks on the D-05 dedicated Basic registry, Linux amd64 and exact Task 4 base/hashlock. Official releases demonstrate published versions, not local installation, API compatibility or build/publication success. Before later deployment, verify exact versions and Bicep build/type diagnostics without API-version substitution; any future build/publication requires separate action authorization/budget and digest proof. No installation or additional compute authorized here. [CLI release](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/release-notes-azure-cli), [Bicep release](https://github.com/Azure/bicep/releases/tag/v0.38.33).
+
+Microsoft recommends at least one native retry for long-running replicas interrupted by maintenance. Accepted parent policy stays zero native retries because orchestration must distinguish confirmed failures from ambiguous launches and centrally limit replay; durable source worksets preserve resumable progress. This is a trade-off: a maintenance-interrupted replica can leave work incomplete, and zero retries is no maintenance guarantee. This disclosure requires review with the finding, not a redundant acceptance gate for the already accepted default; Stage 7 must retain maintenance/failure recovery and one-replay evidence. The recommendation and policy coexist without silently revising either. [Maintenance guidance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/jobs).

