@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Task 5 concrete owner proposal, revision 3
+
+Status: **PROPOSED / UNACCEPTED**. Decider: Lowell Mason. Prepared 2026-10-06 UTC (2026-10-05 Eastern). No provisioning, role assignment, installation, trigger activation or additional SEC access is requested by accepting this documentation proposal. Acceptance must identify this revision and hash; exact answer and root receipt time must be retained separately. Prior production-binding answer was “Keep binding undecided”; this proposal does not override that answer without an explicit new acceptance.
+
+## Proposed decision batch
+
+| Decision | Concrete proposed value | Evidence / implication |
+|---|---|---|
+| D-01 production binding | AzureCloud; tenant `0bb72127-3aa2-408f-a5e4-ba9abcfc6db6`; subscription `3c92a216-8ed6-4897-b741-11ed287b8617` (LGM Consulting) | These are previously observed candidates in `azure-auth-root-report.json`, accepted only for temporary probing so far. Production acceptance is a new decision; effective authority remains Stage 7. |
+| D-02 group | `rg-sec-edgar-dev-eastus` | New dedicated group, preserving accepted region order eastus → eastus2 → centralus. If fallback is necessary, replace the region suffix only through a recorded binding revision. Name availability/policy unproved. |
+| D-03 environment/names/actors | Environment `dev`; stem `sec-edgar-dev`; managed environment `cae-sec-edgar-dev-eastus`; manual job `job-sec-edgar-dev`; ADF `adf-sec-edgar-dev`; workspace `law-sec-edgar-dev`; action group `ag-sec-edgar-dev`; Storage `secedgardevb8617`; ACR `secedgardevb8617`; worker UAMI `id-sec-edgar-dev-worker`; distinct pull UAMI `id-sec-edgar-dev-pull`; ADF system-assigned MI | Names are proposals, globally unique Storage/ACR availability remains Stage 7. Distinct worker/pull identities avoid granting registry push or deployment authority to the worker. Container/table scopes are enumerated in the permission contract, principal IDs deferred. |
+| D-04 operators/authority | Lowell Mason `mason.lowell@mac.com` as deployment/bootstrap/role-assignment and approval/rollback human operator. Bootstrap selects User Access Administrator at the exact D-01 subscription for custom-role definitions and subscription async-observer assignment, plus a proposed custom SecEdgarBootstrap role there with Actions `Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups/read`, `Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups/write`, `Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/providers/read`, `microsoft.app/register/action`, `Microsoft.DataFactory/register/action`, `Microsoft.Storage/register/action`, `Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/register/action`, `Microsoft.ContainerRegistry/register/action`, `Microsoft.OperationalInsights/register/action`, `Microsoft.Insights/Register/Action`. Ongoing deployment selects Contributor + Role Based Access Control Administrator on the exact D-02 RG; approval/rollback receives separate scoped evidence read and approval/pointer Table write roles | These selected delegations are required prerequisites, not observed current assignments. Existing authorized administrator must establish them before deployment; no present Owner/UAA assumption. UAA includes `Microsoft.Authorization/*`, `*/read`, `Microsoft.Support/*`, supplying roleDefinitions/write and roleAssignments/write at subscription for custom runtime roles/async reads. RG roles are a broad trusted-human baseline: Contributor can mutate templates/identities and retrieve account keys; role admin grants privilege. No runtime actor gets these broad roles. Effective allow/deny proof remains Stage 7; app enforces hash-bound approval. Catalog evidence: `provider/task5-permissions/registration-supplement.md`. |
+| D-05 registry | New Basic ACR in the dedicated group/selected region, classic RBAC Registry Permissions mode, anonymous/admin access disabled, public HTTPS | Classic AcrPull is registry-wide; dedicated registry bounds exposure. ABAC/repository role is an alternative requiring explicit revised selection; role-mode mixing is not allowed. [Microsoft ACR roles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-registry/container-registry-rbac-built-in-roles-overview). |
+| D-06 image pull | Distinct user-assigned MI `id-sec-edgar-dev-pull`; AcrPull only at exact registry; registry ARM-token authentication enabled where Container Apps managed-identity pull requires it | Digest pin each worker deployment. [Managed-identity pull](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/managed-identity-image-pull). No credentials obtained here. |
+| D-07 rollback | Retain every deployed worker digest and its manifest/config/platform layers indefinitely during initial development, including each active and prior compatible digest; no automated deletion/untagged retention/purge for them; readable by pull identity; record generation→parser/schema/worker digest association and verify digest availability before rollback | Aligns development artifact retention. A mutable tag or stored digest string alone is insufficient; exact image contents must remain pullable. Publication/rollback compatibility proof remains Stage 7. |
+| D-08 tools/build method | Pin deployment CLI Azure CLI `2.90.0`, Bicep CLI `0.38.33`, `uv 0.12.15` for investigation reproduction. Select future build method: ACR quick tasks on the proposed D-05 dedicated Basic registry, Linux amd64, exact Task 4 Python base child digest and 21-distribution binary-wheel hash lock. No local Docker/buildx is available. Temporary registry is deleted and all four runs exhausted | CLI/uv observed, Bicep absent; official [Bicep release](https://github.com/Azure/bicep/releases/tag/v0.38.33), [CLI release notes](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/release-notes-azure-cli). Documentation acceptance selects method and prerequisites only, authorizes no installation, provisioning, production build/publication, compute or budget. Effective future build permissions/push/digest proof remain Stage 7; no present facility or publication success is claimed. |
+| D-18 application observation | 30-second polling base, honor longer server `Retry-After`; absolute 4,200-second application observation deadline from initial start issuance, including ARM async acceptance and 3,600-second replica allowance | New policy requiring explicit acceptance. Unknown ID/timeout/unavailable status/deadline → `execution_unknown`, no launch retry or transient replay. Exact execution success plus matching successful durable result required. [Jobs Start](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/resource-manager/containerapps/jobs/start?view=rest-resource-manager-containerapps-2026-07-01). |
+| D-14 historical daily recovery gap | Explicitly accept Stage 1's evidence limitation: the 33 listed but uninspected historical middle-quarter daily directories do not establish an outage-recovery horizon. Historical backfill uses quarterly evidence; recovery spanning any of those uninspected daily units requires later bounded evidence and owner authorization before its coverage can be claimed | Proposal is a gap disposition, not a waiver of parent recovery correctness and not authorization for new SEC requests. `source-assessment.md`, D-14 discrepancy. No claim that these 33 directories were inspected, no substitution of list coverage for body/ingestion coverage. A contract revision, if the owner wants a weaker recovery guarantee, requires separately explicit revision acceptance. |
+
+Accepted zero-native-retry default remains authoritative and needs no redundant new decision: Microsoft recommends ≥1 retry for maintenance-interrupted long-running jobs, while centralized orchestration preserves ambiguity safety and at most one confirmed transient replay. This trade-off can leave interrupted work incomplete; Stage 7 maintenance recovery remains required. [Maintenance guidance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/jobs). Revision 1 is preserved immutably in `versions/owner-decision-proposal-r1-b581320fbe3a6de7414a373fb25b457de7c7e21b8e96435aa8511270827b5d9e.md`; D-16/D-17 in that historical proposal collided with existing Task 4 discrepancy IDs and are superseded by D-18 plus this disclosure, not accepted decisions.
+
+Revision 2 is preserved at `versions/owner-decision-proposal-r2-b389b78a3ae72c90f170626d9ff427c554a012d82bd1e99ca8eab1f405848b4b.md`. Its unsupported generic provider registration Action is replaced by the seven verified namespace Actions, and its invented present-facility readiness gate is replaced by a concrete future build-method choice. Neither historical revision was submitted for owner acceptance.
+
+Suggested root three-part batch, with this revision's exact hash:
+
+1. Accept proposed production bindings, names, actor identity types and Lowell's selected broad bootstrap/deployment/approval authority (D-01–D-04), or provide exact replacements. Selection does not confirm current assignments or effective authority.
+2. Accept Basic RBAC ACR, distinct pull UAMI, indefinite digest availability, exact tool pins and future ACR Linux amd64 quick-task build method (D-05–D-08), or provide exact replacements. Actual later facility/build/publication requires separate authorization and Stage 7 evidence.
+3. Accept new 30s/4200s observation policy D-18 and explicitly limited D-14 historical daily recovery-gap disposition, or state revised policy/gap decision. Zero-retry maintenance trade-off is disclosed under the already accepted policy, with Stage 7 proof pending.
+
+A partial answer applies only to identified rows. Silence or a tooling/probe instruction is not acceptance.
+
+Selected documentation API contracts and conservative uncertain-state handling are recorded separately in `azure-contracts.md`; deployment permission/capacity/network/response behavior stays `reserved/not_run` in `stage-7-checks.md`. The accepted parent safeguards, daily overlap, nullable accession, canonical filing_date and closed-quarter withdrawal gate remain authoritative.

