@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Task 5 public permission evidence and proposed matrix
+
+Public documentation collection only, observed 2026-10-06 UTC. No Azure, credential, tenant, SEC or deployment calls were made. JSON files are versioned curated source extracts rather than full page copies; source_version is the documented page update date where available, otherwise the explicitly rolling documentation state. The retrieved_at_utc fields identify collection-batch time anchors, not the exact timestamp of each individual HTTP request. sources-manifest.json contains SHA-256 of the exact retained JSON bytes. Failures are retained in retrieval-failures.json.
+
+This proposal assumes the parent's pending owner proposal: ADF system-assigned managed identity; distinct worker and pull user-assigned managed identities; dedicated registry in RBAC Registry Permissions mode. Concrete resource names, principal IDs and accepted deployment delegation conditions remain owner bindings. API versions are supplied by the sibling contracts work; Azure RBAC permission catalogs themselves are rolling, not API-version-specific.
+
+## Operation matrix
+
+Prefixes below expand literally: B = Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/blobServices/containers/blobs/; T = Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/tableServices/tables/entities/. Unless stated otherwise Actions and DataActions not listed are empty. Custom role definitions are proposals, not deployed or observed roles.
+
+| Actor / identity | Audience | API operations and exact permission set | Proposed role / assignment scope | Network / evidence / Stage 7 proof |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| ADF system-assigned MI | https://management.azure.com/ | Job GET/start and execution GET/list: Actions Microsoft.App/jobs/read, Microsoft.App/jobs/start/action, Microsoft.App/jobs/execution/read, Microsoft.App/jobs/executions/read | Custom job controller role assigned separately to each job resource | ARM HTTPS/DNS/TLS; jobs-actions.json, jobs-trust.json; test allow required operations and deny write/listSecrets |
+| ADF same MI | https://management.azure.com/ | Start Location polling: Actions Microsoft.App/locations/containerappsjoboperationresults/read and Microsoft.App/locations/containerappsjoboperationstatuses/read | Separate custom async observer assignment at subscription scope because documented Location routes are subscription/provider/location resources outside job/RG ancestry | ARM approved Location host/path; jobs-actions.json; actual 202 Location may select one action, remove unused action after Stage 7 verification. Generic locations/operationresults/read and operationstatuses/read are only conditional candidates if returned path uses generic routes |
+| ADF same MI | https://storage.azure.com/ | Get durable JSON result: DataAction B + read | Custom result reader at results container; built-in Storage Blob Data Reader is broader because it includes container reads/user delegation key action | Blob HTTPS/DNS/TLS/firewall; blob-roles.json, storage-operation-mapping.json; exact result read and unrelated container denial |
+| Worker UAMI | https://storage.azure.com/ | Blob GET/list + PUT/upload + lease acquire/renew/release: DataActions B + read, B + write | Custom blob worker assigned separately to raw/workset/result/quarantine/generation and lease containers used by worker | Blob endpoint public egress/firewall; blob-roles.json, lease.json; allow lifecycle, require lease IDs on guarded writes and test lease/CAS failure/takeover |
+| Worker UAMI | https://storage.azure.com/ | Table query/insert/conditional update: DataActions T + read, T + add/action, T + update/action | Custom entity worker at each source/attempt/pointer/approval table the application actually needs. Approval write should be withheld if collector does not own approval creation | Table endpoint; table-roles.json, storage-operation-mapping.json, table-cas.json, table-scope.json; prove 412 on stale ETag, no wildcard/missing If-Match |
+| Pull UAMI | ARM tokens accepted by ACR for Container Apps MI integration; general ACR-specific audience https://containerregistry.azure.net/ | Digest image pull: Action Microsoft.ContainerRegistry/registries/pull/read, no DataActions | AcrPull 7f951dda-4ed3-4680-a7ca-43fe172d538d at dedicated registry in legacy RBAC mode | Registry HTTPS/DNS/TLS and registry data endpoint; acr-roles.json, acr-modes.json, image-pull-arm.json, acr-audiences.json; actual pull with configured identity/digest and unrelated registry denial |
+| Reader, Entra user/group/SP | https://storage.azure.com/ | Active pointer entity read and manifest/data Blob read: DataActions T + read; B + read | Separate custom readers at active-pointer table and manifest/published data containers | Table/Blob reachable; table-scope.json and role extracts; test read and deny mutations |
+| Approval/rollback operator, Entra user/group | https://storage.azure.com/ | Candidate Blob read; pointer/approval entity read/add/update: DataActions B + read; T + read, add/action, update/action | Custom operator; exact candidate containers and pointer/approval tables only | Table/Blob reachable; same extracts; demonstrate hash-bound approval, stale-CAS rejection and rollback contract |
+| Deployment operator Lowell, Entra user | https://management.azure.com/ | Resource creation/update/deletion: Contributor Actions * minus documented NotActions, DataActions empty | Proposed operational baseline Contributor at chosen RG; this is broad management authority, not a minimal custom role | ARM reachable; deployment-authority.json; prove effective required resource operations. Subscription group creation and each required provider registration need independent subscription authority |
+| Role-assignment operator Lowell, Entra user | https://management.azure.com/ | Role assignment PUT/delete/read: Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments/write, Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments/delete, */read; built-in also Microsoft.Support/* | RBAC Administrator at RG with proposed condition restricting allowed roles/principals; additional subscription delegation needed for async observer assignment | rbac-admin.json, rbac-delegation.json; effective allowed/denied assignments and condition proof |
+| Identity attachment operator | https://management.azure.com/ | Assign UAMI requires Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities/*/assign/action at identity plus resource write at target | Custom identity assignment permission or Managed Identity Operator scoped to each UAMI; RG Contributor includes relevant resource writes | identity-assignment.json; actual job attachment and identity selection |
+
+## Limits and trust boundaries
+
+1. Starting a job permits arbitrary execution-template overrides using the secrets and container-available identities. Excluding listSecrets does not contain this authority. ADF start MI and deployment operator must be trusted at worker/pull privilege level. Avoid built-in Jobs Operator/Contributor wildcard action sets.
+2. Blob read+write custom role deliberately omits delete/move/add and management container creation. Blob write authorizes more than leases. Provision containers separately; if DFS ACL/move/append or container lease is later selected, this matrix requires re-review. This collection verifies Blob lease, not Lease Container.
+3. Table entity update permission does not enforce CAS, allowed pointer content, partition/row scope, approval hash or separation of duties. Table-scoped RBAC permits all entities in that table. Container scope likewise permits contained blobs; use separate tables/containers or separately verified Blob ABAC conditions where stronger isolation is required.
+4. RBAC-only AcrPull grants registry-wide image pull. Dedicated single-purpose registry contains that scope. ABAC mode could instead use Repository Reader (metadata/read and content/read DataActions) with a repository condition; catalog list is unnecessary. Mode selection is pending owner acceptance.
+5. General ACR guide recommends disabling ARM-token acceptance, but Container Apps MI pull guide requires it enabled. Preserve enabled for this integration pending real pull proof. Neither successful Entra authentication nor assigned role proves pull success.
+6. Contributor has no DataActions but can obtain storage keys and alter identity-bearing jobs. Its broad management powers must not be presented as inability to access data. RG RBAC Administrator also permits privilege grants unless constrained. A least-privilege custom deployment role requires finalized resource operations and must be authored/verified later; no such role was invented here.
+7. RBAC Administrator cannot create custom role definitions. Custom role bootstrap needs a separate authority including Microsoft.Authorization/roleDefinitions/write at permitted assignable scopes; existing Owner/User Access Administrator can be broader authority. Exact bootstrap principal is unresolved.
+8. Generic Microsoft.App async actions are catalog candidates only; grant only actions matching selected/observed Location route. Subscription scope is a proposed conservative assignment for location APIs; actual authorization and narrower scope feasibility are Stage 7 obligations. No 200/202 response or effective authorization was observed here.
+9. Managed identity does not bypass DNS/TLS, public endpoint routing, firewall, network controls, quotas or policy. Identity endpoints and telemetry egress are sibling network-contract topics; public docs do not prove current tenant reachability.
+
+## Retrieval failures
+
+The unnumbered Update Entity URL returned Internal Error twice. The official update-entity2 URL resolved through search and supplies CAS behavior. The Containers permission catalog returned no Microsoft.App rows; Microsoft.App is in the Compute permission catalog. Both limitations and resolution sources are retained.

