+# Task 5 provider capability and limitations
+
+Current public Microsoft evidence supports the selected manual Container Apps Jobs/ADF/Blob/Table design with explicit uncertainty handling. It does **not** establish effective authorization, capacity, actual 200/202 response shape, ADF output correlation, HNS SDK request behavior, trigger dispatch, log delivery or actual worker fit. Those are recorded `reserved/not_run` in `stage-7-checks.md`. Concrete production selections and the new observation policy require explicit owner acceptance; no proposal silently supersedes “Keep binding undecided.”
+
+Versioned selected resource/method/path/schema contracts are in `azure-contracts.md`. Current claim-specific official extracts and failures are under `provider/task5-contracts/`, `provider/task5-permissions/` and `provider/task5-storage/`, each with retained URL/time/hash metadata. Older `provider/preparation/20261005T230634Z/` remains raw preparation only. Bounded rendered extracts are not complete HTTP response bytes; generic access banners did not authorize or require authentication. Documentation outcomes are distinct from actual deployed behavior.
+
