+
+## Resource/network/log and lifecycle boundaries
+
+The final SDK selection is Blob/Table only, retaining Task 4's exact proven wheel combination. `azure-contracts.md` maps every stored object to Blob creation/upload/read throughout its lifecycle; no DFS Path Create, NFS write, rename/recursive-delete or mixed-API append is selected. HNS file interoperability restrictions require this per-instance discipline; public docs do not prove actual SDK behavior. Blob lease finite durations are 15–60s or infinite; renewal/release/break semantics and Table ETag CAS are documented in storage source notes. Lease break/recovery remains an operator-controlled primitive and does not cancel in-flight SEC requests; parent takeover/fencing obligations remain intact.
+
+GPv2 supports the selected Blob/Table account family; HNS/Hot/ZRS product documentation and candidate US regions are checked separately from subscription registration, selected Jobs profile eligibility, quota, capacity and policy. Consumption 2vCPU/4GiB remains the selected candidate; no resource-profile comparison is performed. Temporary storage applies to Jobs: selected Jobs 2026-07-01 create schema exposes `ContainerResources.ephemeralStorage`, JobTemplate volumes and `StorageType.EmptyDir`; the shared Containers guide explicitly says Jobs executions use the template. These establish documented capability, not a numeric allocation guarantee. The general storage-mounts guide publishes 8GiB for >1vCPU but describes apps; 8GiB for this Job is therefore a candidate capacity assumption requiring exact allocation/readback and usable-capacity/worker-usage proof in Stage 7. No persistent Blob mount is assumed; SDK HTTPS transfers and transient replica storage are the design. Exact excerpts are retained in `provider/task5-contracts/jobs-storage-schema.web-extract.txt` and `jobs-storage-applicability.web-extract.txt`.
+
+Public HTTPS paths: worker SEC `www.sec.gov` under accepted source endpoints (closed during Task 5); account Blob and Table endpoints `*.blob.core.windows.net`/`*.table.core.windows.net`; DFS `*.dfs.core.windows.net` is not required by selected Blob-only lifecycle; managed identity local endpoint plus Entra `login.microsoftonline.com` as required by host/auth flow; ACR registry `*.azurecr.io`, registry data/layer download endpoints and documented CDN/blob endpoints; platform/telemetry endpoints. ADF uses ARM `management.azure.com`, exact approved async status/results URLs and exact Storage Blob result path. Every route requires DNS resolution, valid TLS certificates, outbound443/routing and permitted public endpoint/firewall settings; do not disable certificate validation. ADF's selected Azure integration runtime has to reach ARM/results; worker identity service reachability does not imply external egress success.
+
+Select environment appLogsConfiguration.destination `azure-monitor`, then environment diagnostics categories `ContainerAppConsoleLogs` and `ContainerAppSystemLogs` to a dedicated Log Analytics workspace. Select resource-specific/Dedicated destination with Analytics-plan tables `ContainerAppConsoleLogs` and `ContainerAppSystemLogs`; both current table schemas include `JobName`. ADF Dedicated/resource-specific categories `ActivityRuns`, `PipelineRuns`, `TriggerRuns` map to `ADFActivityRun`, `ADFPipelineRun`, `ADFTriggerRun`. Select workspace default90 days and each of these five tables analytics90/total90; this lies within documented Analytics4–730day and total4–4383day ranges. Console table supports Basic/Auxiliary but neither is selected: Basic analytics is fixed30days and Auxiliary retentionInDays is read-only. Workspace defaults alone do not override prior table-specific settings. Logs can arrive minutes later (ADF documentation allows up to15min); missing immediate records do not prove missing execution. Environment diagnostics supports up to5settings; categories and categoryGroup cannot both be specified. Operational retention is distinct from indefinite ingestion-artifact retention. Scheduled-query log alerts/action-group email target Lowell Mason / mason.lowell@mac.com. Actual category readback, exact Job/execution attribution, ingestion, retention and alert delivery remain Stage7. Source extracts are `provider/task5-contracts/log-retention.web-extract.txt`, `log-routes.web-extract.txt`, `log-tables.web-extract.txt`; storage/network limits are in `provider/task5-storage/storage-source-notes.md`.
+
+Storage collector checkpoint synthesis: `provider/task5-storage/storage-source-notes.md` and `sources-v1.json` are preserved unchanged. The account-create/overview tables directly document StorageV2 Standard_ZRS with HNS and Hot. Table coexistence is a combined GPv2 documentation inference, not an explicit HNS-specific sentence or runtime proof. Availability-zone inventory plus Table ZRS requirements support the three region candidates at documentation level, not a complete per-service regional capability matrix or subscription SKU/capacity observation. Their exact caveats remain visible for technical review. The checkpoint's Jobs/log/retention gaps are superseded only by the claim-specific Jobs schema and newer log sources above; the numeric8GiB Jobs allocation caveat remains. Its generic conditional Delete Blob discussion is not a selected worker permission or retention policy; the final worker map grants read/write and indefinite artifact retention with no lifecycle delete. Public selected networking does not inherit the collector's private-endpoint guidance; no private endpoint configuration is selected.
+
