+# Task 5 provisional investigation report
+
+Status: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS (provisional technical package; checkpoint remains open). Technical contract documentation and storage checkpoint synthesis are prepared for review. Task 5 is not COMPLETE and Task 6 is not authorized by this report. Owner responses to revision 3 parts 2 and 3 remain required: D-05–D-08 registry/pull/rollback/build-method/tool selection, and D-18 observation policy plus D-14 historical daily recovery gap disposition. Only the exact D-01–D-04 answer is accepted, as retained in owner-decision-response-r3-part1.json and immutable R3 proposal hash 038cb2ddcd2ca444d7a3855a4686cb457aa13bd373c767bee854ed657d59f944.
+
+Deliverables are azure-contracts.md, provider-review.md, schedules.md, stage-7-checks.md, current decisions.md/discrepancies.csv, and the exact owner proposal/question/response receipts. Public claim-specific source excerpts, failed retrievals, metadata, publisher SDK tags and permission supplements are retained under provider/task5-contracts and provider/task5-permissions. Original indexed historical bodies and rows remain immutable; new rows point to versioned byte copies under versions. Source/runtime evidence and authoritative specifications/plans/packages were not modified.
+
+The selected Jobs family is non-preview 2026-07-01. Blob SDK 12.31.0 explicitly selects service 2026-04-06; Tables 12.7.0 explicitly selects 2020-12-06. The final object lifecycle uses only Blob-created objects and Blob upload/block/commit/read/lease operations, avoiding HNS DFS-created-object overwrite/block mixing restrictions and preserving Task 4's exact dependency lock. No SDK was added. ADF Web turnOffAsync=true and retry0 expose application-owned correlation/observation; exact effective 200/202 headers/body/async routes and worker results remain Stage 7. Seven documented execution statuses have explicit conservative policies. Zero native retries remains the accepted default; Microsoft's maintenance recommendation and incomplete-work tradeoff are disclosed without inventing redundant approval.
+
+Jobs ephemeral-storage applicability is documented by the selected Job schema's ephemeralStorage and EmptyDir/template fields, with the shared Containers guide describing Jobs templates. The numeric 8GiB guide describes apps and is retained as a candidate capacity assumption, not a verified Jobs allocation. Actual allocation/readback and usable capacity/worker usage are reserved Stage 7. No resource-profile comparison was performed.
+
+Verification performed from repository root: `python3 specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/provider/task5-contracts/offline_checks.py` passed 16 local DST assertions and 278 indexed SHA256 references at 2026-10-06T01:42:48.803863+00:00, exit0. The local environment is Python3.14.7, America/New_York with system tzdata2026c-rearguard; this is not ADF Windows-zone execution evidence. Python compile checks passed for all three offline helper files, exit0. `retain_metadata.py` retained103 source records/10failed retrievals and37 contract artifact hashes, exit0. `update_registers.py` appended11 new immutable references in the final documented batch, preserving existing index bytes. preservation-verification.json proves the original180 pre-Task5 rows exactly unchanged, exact R3 hash unchanged and root .venv/uv.lock absent. review-artifact-inventory.json records review paths/hashes at its generation; it excludes itself and reports its index generation explicitly.
+
+Current official retention guidance resolves the 90-day documentation prerequisite: select workspace90 and five Analytics tables analytics90/total90, within supported ranges. Console/system schemas include JobName, and ADF documented resource-specific mappings are explicit. Actual readback, exact execution attribution, ingestion and alert delivery remain Stage7. The helper's public curl attempt failed DNS in the sandbox; its escalated download waited on approval until interruption. It supplied no new resource or credential evidence. The storage collector checkpoint is retained unchanged in provider/task5-storage, with15official claim extracts and both file hashes verified. GPv2/HNS/Hot/ZRS is directly documented; HNS+Table coexistence and candidate regional zone/ZRS support are explicit combined-documentation inferences. A full per-service regional capability matrix and explicit HNS-specific Table coexistence sentence were not retained. Technical reviewers must assess whether those bounded inferences satisfy the Stage1 documentation requirement; they are not silently promoted to effective proof. Newer Jobs/log/retention sources supersede only the named historical checkpoint gaps.
