+The command uv run ruff check on the two offline helper files failed exit2 because the existing root project's deleted module could not be built. Its full merged tool output is retained in ruff-failed-command.json; stdout/stderr were not independently captured. The invocation unexpectedly created root .venv and uv.lock. Root retained exact creation/birthtime/hash receipts, the 578-byte generated lock (SHA256 4f82b97bb3a10b65ddc0854c10c7e50138dcf056f01856eefcae79abae36f459), and cleanup receipts proving removal of only these newly created side effects. Baseline excluded .venv, so original absence is not asserted from baseline inventory. No package repairs or further project-aware uv checks were run. No lint PASS is claimed.
